NETWORKING HARDWARE - MAIN FUNCTIONS

+------------------+------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------+
| DEVICE           | MAIN FUNCTION                                         | REAL-LIFE EXAMPLE                    |
+------------------+------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------+
| Modem            | Connects the local network to the Internet.          | Used at home to connect to the ISP.  |
| Router           | Directs data between the Internet and devices.       | Used at home to share Internet.      |
| Switch           | Connects multiple wired devices on a LAN.            | Used in an office for PCs/printers.  |
| Access Point     | Provides Wi-Fi access to wireless devices.           | Used in school/office for Wi-Fi.     |
| Network Cable    | Carries data through a wired connection.             | Ethernet cable connects PC to switch.|
+------------------+------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------+



Modem         = Internet connection
Router        = Directs and shares network
Switch        = Connects wired devices
Access Point  = Provides Wi-Fi
Network Cable = Carries data
